WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.978
Welcome to our understanding shipping settings training.

00:00:02.978 --> 00:00:04.680
In this video we'll

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.580
discuss what the customer delivery promise is, how your shipping settings

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.315
impact it, what shipping settings are, and how you can configure them.

00:00:12.315 --> 00:00:13.560
By the end of

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.160
the video you'll know how to configure your general shipping settings and

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.413
identify how they'll affect your customer delivery promise.

00:00:20.413 --> 00:00:22.040
When shopping in the

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.000
Amazon store a customer sees a specific date or date range of when a product can

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.216
be expected to arrive on a product detail page.

00:00:30.216 --> 00:00:32.360
That date or date range is

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.858
what we call a customer delivery promise.

00:00:34.858 --> 00:00:37.000
The customer delivery promise for a

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.640
product is composed of handling time, transit time, and a small buffer in case

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.937
of the unexpected like inclement weather.

00:00:43.937 --> 00:00:47.000
Keep in mind that non-business days such

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.877
as weekends and holidays can also impact your handling time.

00:00:50.877 --> 00:00:52.040
This is why

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:55.360
configuring your shipping settings can help you meet your customer delivery

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:55.747
promises.

00:00:55.747 --> 00:00:59.620
Shipping settings are the delivery options you can configure to

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.170
determine your customer delivery promise.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.720
Your shipping settings have two

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.549
sections your shipping templates and your general shipping settings.

00:01:08.549 --> 00:01:09.400
In this

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.455
video we'll specifically focus on general shipping settings.

00:01:12.455 --> 00:01:13.600
To learn more

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.782
about shipping templates check out our video Understand Shipping Templates.

00:01:17.782 --> 00:01:18.200
In

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.480
Seller Central click the gear icon in the upper right corner and then click

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.253
shipping settings.

00:01:23.253 --> 00:01:27.120
From here you'll see two tabs the general shipping settings

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.690
tab and the shipping templates tab.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.260
By clicking the general shipping settings

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:36.120
tab you can review and edit your shipping information such as your default

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.240
shipping address, order fulfillment settings, handling time, and holiday

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.052
shipping schedules.

00:01:41.052 --> 00:01:44.300
Under default shipping address you can configure the

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:47.573
primary physical location you use for shipping orders.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:48.800
Also under order

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.520
fulfillment settings you can configure your general fulfillment settings as

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.900
well as settings for shipping region automation.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.600
You can adjust your cutoff

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.680
time settings either by day of the week or by carrier.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.080
You can also adjust settings

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.240
for weekend operations and deliveries.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.400
Adjusting your weekend delivery settings

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.400
can help shorten your customer delivery promise if your business is open and if

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.575
the carriers you use ship products on weekends.

00:02:12.575 --> 00:02:14.560
Under the handling time section

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.300
you can set your default handling time for your account to either one or two

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:18.551
days.

00:02:18.551 --> 00:02:22.320
This will be the number of days you have to package and hand your products

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.480
over to your carrier.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.960
This will apply to all of your products unless you set an

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.695
asin-specific handling time for that product.

00:02:29.695 --> 00:02:32.040
You can also set an order

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.840
handling capacity which is the number of orders you can manage per day within

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.206
your default handling time.

00:02:37.206 --> 00:02:40.280
Any order above this limit will receive one more

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.880
day of handling time without being considered a late shipment.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:44.600
In the

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.433
holidays section you can see which days Amazon considers holidays.

00:02:48.433 --> 00:02:49.200
These won't

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.962
count as operating days unless you decide to enable them.

00:02:51.962 --> 00:02:53.620
You can also take a tour

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.491
of your shipping settings page by clicking take the tour.

00:02:56.491 --> 00:02:57.640
Make sure to check

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.080
out our help pages on how to create new shipping templates or to edit existing

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:02.578
ones.

00:03:02.578 --> 00:03:07.560
Other help pages also explain weekend carrier operations and holiday

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:07.963
settings.

00:03:07.963 --> 00:03:12.400
In this video you've learned about the customer delivery promise what

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.480
settings affect it and how to navigate the general shipping settings tab in

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.131
Seller Central.

00:03:17.131 --> 00:03:21.040
Make sure to return to the shipping settings page to review and

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.467
update your settings and templates as needed.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.200
This concludes our training on

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.291
shipping settings.

00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:29.633
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
